    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "questionText": "Two blocks \ud835\udc34 and \ud835\udc35 of masses 6 kg and 3 kg rest on a smooth horizontal surface as shown in the figure. If coefficient of friction between \ud835\udc34 and \ud835\udc35 is 0.4, the maximum horizontal force which can make them move without separation is",
    "options": [
      "72 N",
      "40 N",
      "36 N",
      "20 N"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": 2,
    "explanation": "Maximum frictional force on block \ud835\udc35 is \ud835\udf07\ud835\udc5a\ud835\udc35g = 0.4 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 10 = 12 N Hence, maximum acceleration = 12 3 = 4 ms\u22121 Hence, maximum force \ud835\udc39= (\ud835\udc5a\ud835\udc34+ \ud835\udc5a\ud835\udc35)\ud835\udc4e= (6 + 3) \u00d7 4 = 36 N Aliter: We can also apply the formula discussed in previous problem by putting \ud835\udf072 = 0 and \ud835\udf071 = 0.4",
