    "questionText": "A ball of mass \ud835\udc5a moving with a velocity \ud835\udc62 rebounds from a wall. The collision is assumed to be elastic and the force of interaction between the ball and wall varies as shown in the figure. Then the value of \ud835\udc390 is",
    "options": [
      "\ud835\udc5a\ud835\udc62/\ud835\udc47",
      "2 \ud835\udc5a\ud835\udc62/\ud835\udc47",
      "4 \ud835\udc5a\ud835\udc62/\ud835\udc47",
      "\ud835\udc5a\ud835\udc62/2 \ud835\udc47"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": 2,
    "explanation": "Area under the force\u2212 time graph is impulse, and impulse is change in momentum Area of graph=change in momentum \u21d21 2 \ud835\udc47\ud835\udc390 = 2 \ud835\udc5a\ud835\udc62 \u21d2\ud835\udc390 = 4\ud835\udc5a\ud835\udc62 \ud835\udc47",
    "tags": [
      "Laws of Motion",
      "NTA Question Bank",
      "NEET 2026"
    ],
